<http://data.silknow.org/object/2159976a-0791-380f-a7b2-88d960d182c9>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "embroidered, 1800s, Persian; Whitework"@en , "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches, needleweaving and pulled thread work; whitework; bound with block printed cotton.\nThe central are is left mainly undecorated except for two small diagonal corner units at the lower end which are patterned with a ground of needleweaving and multi-petalled flowerheads. At the top a pulled thread section with a needlewoven rectangle, of  joined stars, edged with rows of tiny hexagons in the shape of lozenges [a].  On the two short sides of the rectangle a triangular section repeats the patterning of the lower end.\nA band of needleweaving of [a] on a large scale frames the whole rectangle and is finished wither side with a tiny reciprocal trefoil border in straight stitch.\n\nCotton thread: Z-spun\nEmbroidery Thread: white silk; 2S\nBinding: a narrow block printed cotton binding has been applied around all foru sides.  White ground with an incomplete pattern of small flowerheads in blue or red and pink."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b14325f3-d011-3d4d-b35a-89ffbc819445> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches, needleweaving and pulled thread work; whitework; bound with block printed cotton.\nThe central are is left mainly undecorated except for two small diagonal corner units at the lower end which are patterned with a ground of needleweaving and multi-petalled flowerheads. At the top a pulled thread section with a needlewoven rectangle, of  joined stars, edged with rows of tiny hexagons in the shape of lozenges [a].  On the two short sides of the rectangle a triangular section repeats the patterning of the lower end.\nA band of needleweaving of [a] on a large scale frames the whole rectangle and is finished wither side with a tiny reciprocal trefoil border in straight stitch.\n\nCotton thread: Z-spun\nEmbroidery Thread: white silk; 2S\nBinding: a narrow block printed cotton binding has been applied around all foru sides.  White ground with an incomplete pattern of small flowerheads in blue or red and pink."@en , "embroidered, 1800s, Persian; Whitework"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/2159976a-0791-380f-a7b2-88d960d182c9/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/2159976a-0791-380f-a7b2-88d960d182c9/dimension/2> ;
